-- ===== ccc20 seat questions =====
-- SEAT20-1 a private person arrested me and delivered me to a peace officer; 25 hours since the arrest, 23 hours since delivery: the hours that run against the 24-hour period are 23 (s 503(2), L11210)
#ASSERT (`Under section 503(2), how many hours of the 24-hour period have run against me` TRUE 25 23) EQUALS 23
-- SEAT20-2 I am charged with murder (listed in s 469), taken before a justice, no guilty plea, the prosecutor has not shown cause: the justice is not required to make a release order without conditions: FALSE (s 515(1), L11367; the 'other than an offence in 469' carve-out is a case-by-case kind)
#ASSERT (`Under section 515(1), must the justice make a release order without conditions` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)
-- SEAT20-3 a judge decided my review on 1 January 2025 and I apply again on 30 January 2025 (day 29) without leave: a further application is barred TRUE (s 520(8), L11594; period fixed in the text's own words)
#ASSERT (`Under section 520(8), is a further application by me barred` TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 30 1 2025) FALSE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
-- SEAT20-4 I waived my right to a hearing in writing and the judge received the waiver before the 90 days expired: the custodian is not required to apply TRUE (s 525(1.1), L11730)
#ASSERT (`Under section 525(1.1), is the person having my custody not required to make the application` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
-- SEAT20-5 a peace officer believes I am in a dwelling-house, conditions for a warrant exist, and exigent circumstances make a warrant impracticable: may enter without a warrant TRUE (s 529.3(1), L11807)
#ASSERT (`Under section 529.3(1), may a peace officer enter the dwelling-house without a warrant to arrest or apprehend me` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
-- SEAT20-6 charged with a summary-conviction-only offence; the officer believes the public interest may be satisfied without arresting me and has no grounds to think I will fail to attend: may issue an appearance notice TRUE (s 497(c), L11118)
#ASSERT (`Under section 497, may a peace officer who is barred by section 495(2) from arresting me issue me an appearance notice` `an offence punishable on summary conviction` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
-- SEAT20-7 a judge endorsed the information on 1 January 2025 that no process was to be issued: the last day for commencing proceedings to compel is 1 June 2025 (five months after, s 507.1(5), L11281)
#ASSERT (`Under section 507.1(5), what is the last day for commencing proceedings to compel the issue of a summons or warrant` (Date 1 1 2025)) EQUALS (Date 1 7 2025)  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was EQUALS (Date 1 6 2025); SCENARIO: the reviewer's own mistake: s 507.1(5) says 'not later than six months after the endorsement', the reviewer wrote five months from memory without re-reading; 1 January 2025 plus six months is 1 July 2025, the encoder's answer; no Guide sentence applies

